 on  where the rubber meets the road at the  point where the immune cells are  interacting  at the the invasive front of the tumor  and and how effective or non-effective  are those  so in summary the major problems  in cancer including better treatment of  aggressive and metastatic disease  reducing  over diagnosis and overtreatment disease  and finding  real pre-cancers very early these  nascent lethal pre-cancers  that are defined at least in part by  a very early evidence of immune escape  as well as immune  stromal interaction are  possible using some of these new  technologies  for research and translation i showed  you a lot of multiplex  immunohistochemistry sort of a blend of  flow cytometry  and conventional histology i showed you  some single cell  rna sequence data and that's becoming  more and more important  important in research and giving us more  targets to  handle these but as you saw this becomes  a very big picture big data problem  which requires new  computing and informatics tools to  handle both of those  and it takes a team of the blind  scientists and a chance to put them  together to make meaningful progress so  with that  i'll acknowledge all of my collaborators  and co-investigators  as well as the funders and the industry  partners that have made  all this possible and i'm happy to take  any questions
 

